l-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"true\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-controls=\"application-description-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >Application description<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                            <li id=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy\" class=\"inactive eael-tab-item-trigger eael-tab-nav-item\" aria-selected=\"false\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"tab\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-controls=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy-tab\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                            \n                            \n                            \n                                                            <span class=\"eael-tab-title title-after-icon\" >FT-IR spectroscopy<\/span>                                                    <\/li>\n                                    <\/ul>\n            <\/div>\n            \n            <div class=\"eael-tabs-content\">\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"application-description-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"application-description-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <p>From a security and defense perspective, it is absolutely essential to have a fast and reliable technique that can analyze potentially hazardous chemicals, including gaseous samples. For this reason, <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/ft-ir-spectroscopy\/\"><strong>FT-IR spectroscopy<\/strong><\/a> is more than suitable, because it is not only a highly specific method (each substance has its own unique spectrum), but it can also provide information about functional groups. In addition, it can be combined with other techniques: e.g. <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/ftir-gc\/\"><strong>gas chromatography (GC)<\/strong><\/a>.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_9609\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-9609\" style=\"width: 600px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9609\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/d8edd7e7-300x296.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"591\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/d8edd7e7-300x296.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/d8edd7e7-1024x1009.png 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/d8edd7e7-768x757.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/d8edd7e7.png 1082w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 600px) 100vw, 600px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-9609\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">FT-IR spectroscopy and gas chromatography (GC) connection scheme<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Each instrument is equipped with spectral libraries with tens of thousands of spectra of various substances, so you only need to measure the spectrum and the search algorithm itself identifies the measured spectrum and informs you about its danger, in just a few moments. You get not only an accurate and reliable result, but also time that can save lives.<\/p>\n<p> [{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_-1_0} id=&#8221;attachment_9611&#8243; align=&#8221;{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_-1_1}&#8221; width=&#8221;{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_-1_2}&#8221;]<img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9611\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/95e5245e-300x213.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_0_-1_1}\" height=\"{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_0_-1_2}\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/95e5245e-300x213.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/95e5245e-1024x727.png 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/95e5245e-768x545.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/95e5245e.png 1467w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/> FT-IR spectrum of GA warfare gas with a significant band around 2200 cm<sup>-1<\/sup>, which is typical for cyanides[\/{wpml_trans_unit_2_0_4_-1_0}]<figure id=\"attachment_9613\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-9613\" style=\"width: 500px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-9613\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/7b02de6e-300x222.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"369\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/7b02de6e-300x222.png 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/7b02de6e-1024x757.png 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/7b02de6e-768x567.png 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/10\/7b02de6e.png 1409w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-9613\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">FT-IR spectrum of the warfare gas which contains a pinacoyl group, and thus shows more pronounced bands in the area of valence vibrations (about 3000 cm<sup>-1<\/sup>)<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/p>\n                    <\/div>\n\t\t        \n                    <div id=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy-tab\" class=\"clearfix eael-tab-content-item inactive\" data-title-link=\"ft-ir-spectroscopy-tab\">\n\t\t\t\t        <style>@media(max-width:1024px){.elementor-6756 .elementor-element.elementor-element-43f4b2a9 .dce-post-item{padding:0px 0px 20px 0px;}}@media(max-width:767px){.elementor-6756 .elementor-element.elementor-element-43f4b2a9 .dce-post-item{padding:0px 0px 15px 0px;}}<\/style>\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"section\" data-elementor-id=\"6756\" class=\"elementor elementor-6756 elementor-5032\" data-elementor-post-type=\"elementor_library\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-66c51c3 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"66c51c3\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-no\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-c